<title>USA: U.S. business loans fell $82 mln in Sept 11 week.</title>
<headline>U.S. business loans fell $82 mln in Sept 11 week.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commercial and industrial loans on the books of U.S. commercial banks, excluding acceptances, fell $82 million to $360.19 billion in the week ended Sept 11, the Federal Reserve said Friday.</p>
<p>Including acceptances, loans fell $91 million to $361.9 billion, the Fed said.</p>
</text>
